<%# FR-OSS-01: on every page, small and non-intrusive; not an ad surface and never
    used to ask for consent. Identical for every viewer, so it is safe on the
    cached word shell. FR-OSS-02: the close control is revealed by oss-banner.js,
    which keeps the dismissal in localStorage for 30 minutes — no cookie. Without
    JavaScript the banner simply stays. %>
<aside class="oss-banner" data-oss-banner aria-label="About PronounceAll">
  <p class="oss-banner__text">
    PronounceAll is open-source and free.
    <a href="https://github.com/alpkavakli/PronounceAll">See the code on GitHub</a>
  </p>
  <button type="button" class="oss-banner__close" data-oss-banner-close hidden>
    Close<span class="visually-hidden"> the open-source notice</span>
  </button>
</aside>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <p>
    PronounceAll is free software under the
    <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html">AGPL-3.0</a>.
    Content is licensed
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <%# FR-IPA-10 places the cross-variant index in the FOOTER on purpose: in
        v1.0 it renders the same rows as the per-variant page, so a contextual
        in-page link would lead somewhere identical. The footer is the stable,
        low-traffic surface for readers who genuinely want the global view. %>
    <a href="/learnIPA">Learn IPA</a>
    ·
    <a href="/practice">Practice</a>
    ·
    <%# Static and identical for every viewer, so it is safe on the cached
        shell: /login itself says whether you are signed in. %>
    <a href="/login">Account</a>
    ·
    <a href="/settings">Settings</a>
    ·
    <a href="https://github.com/alpkavakli/PronounceAll">Source code</a>
  </p>
</footer>
<script type="module" src="/js/oss-banner.js"></script>
